<p>It's important to sync all user interactions with the server, even if mu=
ltiple interactions occur on the same post. This data can provide valuable =
insights for analysis. To handle potential conflicts, we can employ the "la=
st write wins" strategy.</p>
<p>In our local database, we add a new UserInteractions table to store all =
user interactions. Once an interaction successfully syncs with the server, =
the Posts Repository removes it from the UserInteractions table, and update=
s the corresponding entry in the Posts table.</p>
<p>We represent the database tables in the data layer design (Figure 7) as =
Data Access Objects (DAO) components.</p>
